  "problem": "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y={2}^{x}?$ \n\n- $(0,10]$\n- $[0,10]$\n- $(0,\\infty )$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $(0,10]$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[0,10]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[0,10].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $(0,\\infty )$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
